PUBLIC RECORD

=20

TO THE RT HON SIR STEPHEN COBB, PRESIDENT OF THE FAMILY DIVISION=20

=20

WHERE IS THE EVIDENCE?

=20

A Formal Request for Determination of Paragraph 64 of DH v RH (No 3) [2024]=
 EWFC 79 =E2=80=94 Addressed to the Rt Hon Sir Stephen Cobb, President of the Fami=
ly Division =E2=80=94 Copied to Commissioner Sir Mark Rowley QPM, Metropolitan Pol=
ice Service

=20

Case references
BV20D01752  |  CA-2024-001342  |  AC-2025-LON-004293  |  BL-2024-001217  | =
 FA-2026-000019

=20

=20

Dear Sir Stephen,

=20

I write in your capacity as President of the Family Division. This letter i=
s copied to Commissioner Sir Mark Rowley QPM because the matters to which it=
 relates are also the subject of an existing criminal referral to the Metrop=
olitan Police Service.

=20

I am an autistic litigant in person with a co-occurring diagnosis of Post-T=
raumatic Stress Disorder. During the ten-day final hearing in BV20D01752 (19=
=E2=80=9328 February 2024), the court repeatedly recognised my autism and PTSD and=
 operated throughout the hearing under FPR Part 3A participation measures gr=
anted in consequence of those disabilities. The contemporaneous attendance n=
otes of the hearing (Ex47) record twenty-five references to autism and PTSD,=
 including thirteen made by the trial judge himself.

=20

The judgment that followed, DH v RH (No 3) [2024] EWFC 79, contains no refe=
rence to autism, PTSD, disability, vulnerability, participation measures, or=
 FPR Part 3A. The attendance notes and the judgment therefore describe the s=
ame proceedings in materially different terms.

=20

Paragraph 64 of that judgment nevertheless characterises my presentation in=
 the witness box as having "bordered on the concerning" and states that I ha=
d become "obsessed" with demonstrating the existence of hidden assets. This =
finding is unsubstantiated as confirmed in the oral evidence (Ex47).

=20

The issue raised by this letter is not whether the financial remedy outcome=
 was correct or incorrect. Nor is it a request to revisit the merits of the =
proceedings. It is a narrower question concerning the relationship between t=
he contemporaneous evidential record and the findings recorded in the judgme=
nt.

=20

I therefore respectfully ask the President of the Family Division to determ=
ine the following single question of fact:

=20

THE QUESTION

=20

Is there evidence within Ex47, the contemporaneous record of the oral evide=
nce given during the ten-day final hearing, that corroborates the findings r=
ecorded at paragraph 64 of DH v RH (No 3) [2024] EWFC 79?

=20

The question admits of one of two answers.

=20
If the answer is yes, I respectfully request identification of the specific=
 passage or passages relied upon, by page and line reference.
=20
If the answer is no, I respectfully request confirmation that no such corro=
borating passage has been identified.
=20

The significance of the question is straightforward. The findings recorded =
at paragraph 64 have subsequently formed part of a chain of judicial charact=
erisations that continue to carry substantial procedural, financial, and rep=
utational consequences. If those findings are supported by the contemporaneo=
us evidential record, the supporting evidence should be identifiable. If the=
y are not, that fact should be capable of clear determination.

=20

In accordance with the communication adjustments recommended by the Central=
 London Adult Autism Service, I respectfully request a clear, direct, and un=
ambiguous response addressing the specific question posed.

=20

I respectfully request a substantive reply within seven days of the date of=
 this letter, namely by 4 June 2026.

=20

=20

=20

Yours sincerely,

=20

Nadia Zahmoul

Litigant in Person

28 May 2026

Veritas Numquam Perit

