Normal"><b><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></b></p><p class=3D"MsoNormal">Dear Sir Stephen,<o=
:p></o:p></p><p class=3D"MsoNormal"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p><p class=3D"MsoNormal">=
I write in your capacity as President of the Family Division. This letter is=
 copied to Commissioner Sir Mark Rowley QPM because the matters to which it =
relates are also the subject of an existing criminal referral to the Metropo=
litan Police Service.<o:p></o:p></p><p class=3D"MsoNormal"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></=
p><p class=3D"MsoNormal">I am an autistic litigant in person with a co-occurri=
ng diagnosis of Post-Traumatic Stress Disorder. During the ten-day final hea=
ring in BV20D01752 (19=E2=80=9328 February 2024), the court repeatedly recognised =
my autism and PTSD and operated throughout the hearing under FPR Part 3A par=
ticipation measures granted in consequence of those disabilities. The contem=
poraneous attendance notes of the hearing (Ex47) record twenty-five referenc=
es to autism and PTSD, including thirteen made by the trial judge himself.<o=
:p></o:p></p><p class=3D"MsoNormal"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p><p class=3D"MsoNormal">=
The judgment that followed, <i>DH v RH (No 3)</i> [2024] EWFC 79, contains n=
o reference to autism, PTSD, disability, vulnerability, participation measur=
es, or FPR Part 3A. The attendance notes and the judgment therefore describe=
 the same proceedings in materially different terms.<o:p></o:p></p><p class=3D=
"MsoNormal"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p><p class=3D"MsoNormal">Paragraph 64 of that j=
udgment nevertheless characterises my presentation in the witness box as hav=
ing <i>&quot;bordered on the concerning&quot;</i> and states that I had beco=
me <i>&quot;obsessed&quot;</i> with demonstrating the existence of hidden as=
sets. This finding is unsubstantiated as confirmed in the oral evidence (Ex4=
7).<o:p></o:p></p><p class=3D"MsoNormal"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p><p class=3D"MsoNor=
mal">The issue raised by this letter is not whether the financial remedy out=
come was correct or incorrect. Nor is it a request to revisit the merits of =
the proceedings. It is a narrower question concerning the relationship betwe=
en the contemporaneous evidential record and the findings recorded in the ju=
dgment.<o:p></o:p></p><p class=3D"MsoNormal"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p><p class=3D"Ms=
oNormal">I therefore respectfully ask the President of the Family Division t=
o determine the following single question of fact:<o:p></o:p></p><p class=3D"M=
soNormal"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p><p class=3D"MsoNormal"><b>THE QUESTION</b><o:p>=
</o:p></p><p class=3D"MsoNormal"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p><p class=3D"MsoNormal"><b>=
Is there evidence within Ex47, the contemporaneous record of the oral eviden=
ce given during the ten-day final hearing, that corroborates the findings re=
corded at paragraph 64 of <i>DH v RH (No 3)</i> [2024] EWFC 79?<o:p></o:p></=
b></p><p class=3D"MsoNormal"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p><p class=3D"MsoNormal">The que=
stion admits of one of two answers.<o:p></o:p></p><p class=3D"MsoNormal"><o:p>=
&nbsp;</o:p></p><ul style=3D"margin-top:0cm" type=3D"disc"><li class=3D"MsoNormal"=
 style=3D"mso-list:l1 level1 lfo3">If the answer is <b>yes</b>, I respectfully=
 request identification of the specific passage or passages relied upon, by =
page and line reference.<o:p></o:p></li></ul><p class=3D"MsoNormal"><o:p>&nbsp=
;</o:p></p><ul style=3D"margin-top:0cm" type=3D"disc"><li class=3D"MsoNormal" styl=
e=3D"mso-list:l1 level1 lfo3">If the answer is <b>no</b>, I respectfully reque=
st confirmation that no such corroborating passage has been identified.<o:p>=
</o:p></li></ul><p class=3D"MsoNormal"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p><p class=3D"MsoNorma=
l">The significance of the question is straightforward. The findings recorde=
d at paragraph 64 have subsequently formed part of a chain of judicial chara=
cterisations that continue to carry substantial procedural, financial, and r=
eputational consequences. If those findings are supported by the contemporan=
eous evidential record, the supporting evidence should be identifiable. If t=
hey are not, that fact should be capable of clear determination.<o:p></o:p><=
/p><p class=3D"MsoNormal"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p><p class=3D"MsoNormal">In accorda=
nce with the communication adjustments recommended by the Central London Adu=
lt Autism Service, I respectfully request a clear, direct, and unambiguous r=
esponse addressing the specific question posed.<o:p></o:p></p><p class=3D"MsoN=
ormal"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p><p class=3D"MsoNormal">I respectfully request a su=
bstantive reply within seven days of the date of this letter, namely by <b>4=
 June 2026</b>.<o:p></o:p></p><p class=3D"MsoNormal"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p><p c=
